{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-action-discipline", "file": "references/demo-evidence-checkpoint.md", "content": "# Demo evidence checkpoint in capped Continual-ARC tasks

A demo response should change the solver's evidence state before it triggers another action. For each returned pair, record the exact input/output delta, salient unchanged cells or objects, and how the observation updates or contradicts candidate rules. Compare the new example with all earlier pairs; do not assume a visually different pair belongs to a different task rule, but do not force a unified explanation if replay fails.

Before requesting another demo, identify at least two test-relevant hypotheses consistent with the evidence and state the precise observation that would separate them. If no useful discriminator is apparent, stop requesting and choose the best supported submission. Avoid consecutive requests without an intervening evidence analysis. This gate is especially important when each request costs an action and submission feedback is only binary.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545531/attempts/bc528d856f1a41f1a28c3fa14e5fbbd6/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzles/continual-arc-action-discipline/references/demo-evidence-checkpoint.md"}
